# independently of tools/ucd/gen_tables.py. This file is the
# oracle tests/unit/test_sweep.cpp checks the compiled tables
# against, over all 1,114,112 codepoints, with no network and no
# Python at test time (documentation/design.md section 12.1).
#
# Each line is a property, the number of maximal ranges over which
# its value is constant, and FNV-1a-64 over the text of those
# ranges: "%06X..%06X <value long name>\n" per range. The value is
# spelled, never numbered, so that a renumbered enum fails here.
#
# "partition" is the record's own boundary set - every property the
# record holds - hashed as "%06X\n" per boundary. The library's runs
# table must reproduce it exactly, which is what set.h's agreement
# with char.h rests on.
#
# To localise a failure:
#   tools/ucd/gen_sweep.py --property Script > /tmp/oracle
#   GUNI_SWEEP_DUMP=Script build/.../testSweep > /tmp/ours
#   diff /tmp/oracle /tmp/ours
